# C++ Constructor and Destructor

## Description

This program demonstrates the use of a constructor and destructor in C++. The constructor is automatically called when an object is created, while the destructor is automatically called when the object is destroyed.

## Class Used

### 1. Demo

The `Demo` class contains a constructor and a destructor.

### Constructor

The `Demo()` constructor displays the message `Constructor called` when an object is created.

### Destructor

The `~Demo()` destructor displays the message `Destructor called` when the object is destroyed.

## Main Function

The `main()` function creates an object named `d` of the `Demo` class.

When the object is created, the constructor is automatically executed.

When the `main()` function ends, the object is destroyed and the destructor is automatically executed.

## Output

Constructor called
Destructor called

## OOP Concept Used

- Constructor
- Destructor
- Object Creation
- Automatic Object Cleanup

## Program Flow

Start
  ↓
Create Demo Object
  ↓
Constructor Called
  ↓
Program Execution
  ↓
Object Destroyed
  ↓
Destructor Called
  ↓
End